Maddie (docs): Quick ask: we need a tiny, go-focused example for the error-ref explaining how to handle 429s that may return partial content. Keep it terse — 1-paragraph + a 6-8 line snippet.

Carlos (sdk-go): I can do a Go snippet. Idea: detect 429, honor Retry-After >=1s, otherwise bounded backoff, drop oldest non-system turns until under target token estimate. Will keep names short.

Ivy (eng-runtime): FYI runtime sets x-partial-ok when we served partial content and surfaces partialResponse in the SDK error. Recommend logging that and avoiding re-applying side-effects until you reconcile. Also treat Retry-After <1s as ignore.

Bea (qa): Add a one-line smoke test note: replay a conversation with a simulated 429 + x-partial-ok and verify idempotency for side-effecting flows. I'll add the test case.

Carlos (sdk-go): Draft snippet (Go):

```go
// trim oldest non-system turns, honor Retry-After, retry up to 3 times
func SendWithTrim(client *sdk.Client, convo []*Message, target int) (*Response, error) {
 for attempts:=0; attempts<3; attempts++ {
  resp, err := client.Generate(convo)
  if err==nil { return resp, nil }
  if err.Status!=429 { return nil, err }
  ra := parseRetryAfter(err.Headers.Get("Retry-After"))
  sleep(time.Duration(chooseDelay(ra, attempts)))
  // drop oldest non-system messages until estimate < target
  for len(convo)>0 && tokenEstimate(convo)>target {
    if convo[0].Role=="system" { break }
    convo = convo[1:]
  }
 }
 return nil, fmt.Errorf("retries exhausted")
}
```

Carlos (sdk-go): I'll include a short comment in the PR linking to sdk-go/retry/util and the docs page.

Ivy (eng-runtime): Add callout text: "Do not remove system/instruction messages." Also: "If err.PartialResponse != nil or x-partial-ok==1, surface a reconciliation step before replaying side-effects."

Maddie (docs): Perfect. I'll write a one-paragraph explanation and the callouts, then open a small PR to docs. Please tag @Carlos and @Bea for reviews.

